WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.850
People need somewhere safe to practice, and
that's harder to arrange than it sounds.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.465
Many staff won't qualify for a
developer sandbox on their own,

3
00:00:08.465 --> 00:00:12.225
and those sandboxes don't exist
in the government clouds at all.

4
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:16.530
So the program's approach has two steps:
practice in a commercial sandbox,

5
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:21.265
then rehearse once in the agency's own
non-production government tenant before

6
00:00:21.265 --> 00:00:26.000
each gate, where a feature difference shows
up as a finding instead of a surprise.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.787
Every lab follows the same rules:
never production, never real data.

8
00:00:30.787 --> 00:00:34.819
The decision for the program office:
arrange lab tenants centrally,

9
00:00:34.819 --> 00:00:38.850
including that government rehearsal
tenant, before the first labs.

10
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.110
Next, the largest group of all.
